id: pm-brand-semantic-asset-change-reports
title: Explain semantic changes between generated SVG assets
description: "Read-only, bounded SVG review evidence for visible text, token roles, geometry and accessible labels."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: assets,cli,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-29T00:47:34.875Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-29T01:05:03.070Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Attribute reordering yields zero semantic changes; a changed status color and truncated label yield two localized findings; no raster generation or network is needed; typed SDK and CLI expose bounded JSON and TOON with typed refusals and remedies; validate public tracker assets on a read-only non-git copy.
comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-29T00:47:58.698Z",codex-agent,"Overlap rechecked against installed pm SDK declarations, pm-brand generators and diagnostics, pm-vcs vcs diff, pm-gantt-chart rendering, and pm-graph snapshot impact. No SVG semantic comparator exists. pm-vcs owns versioned bytes and generic diffs; this feature supplies bounded static asset review evidence. Reuse the existing lazy public SDK loader, attachOutputTokenAccounting and TOON encoder. Pure read-only input/output: no tracker writes, journal, imports, sync, status interpretation or shared mutable state in the product path; transaction isolation is not claimed. Unsupported SVG constructs will refuse with a remedy rather than silently omit rendering effects."
  "2026-10-29T01:01:59.105Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed compareSemanticAssets/renderSemanticAssetReport plus semantic-diff CLI, strict bounded static SVG grammar, grouped visible outline metadata and geometry digests, localized text/token/geometry/accessibility evidence, JSON/TOON output via SDK accounting, typed refusals and remedies. Focused 15/15 tests, typecheck, lint and docstrings passed. New modules measured 100/100/100/100 coverage. The 500-sequence model completed 6000 transitions, 997 older-input replays and 500 complete native SDK read-backs with relationships, fields and ambient focus preserved. Behavioral reverts caught 4/4 independent faults; restored implementation passed the unchanged regressions. Public read-only non-git tracker: 16 items, 48 generated source assets, 48 comparisons (16 identity/0 changes, 16 serialization/0 changes, 16 edits/32 findings), 96 reports, max 94 SDK estimated tokens/375 bytes, zero budget refusals; SDK state and byte hashes unchanged. See docs/semantic-assets-validation.md. Runtime is read-only and creates no import/export/sync journal, idempotency key, claim, lease or shared product state. No transaction-isolation or atomic snapshot claim; each supplied SVG string is caller-owned input. Full npm/Bun release gates are delegated to exact-head CI per the host resource constraint."
  "2026-10-29T01:04:57.911Z",codex-agent,"Ready-for-review PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brand/pull/27 . Linked tests ran through pinned pm: 1/1 command passed, 15/15 tests, zero skips/failures. Test-result tracking is disabled by the existing project policy, so this comment records the successful run without changing that policy. Isolated-home strict tracker health passed; the ordinary home exposed an ambient pm-github host-version mismatch (pinned host versus newer global extension), not tracker corruption. Four behavioral reverts passed again after final implementation changes; two image regressions passed. All 52 generated banners match main byte-for-byte after removing only the new data-text metadata. Extended numeric fuzz checks geometry coordinate, size and opacity domains as well as input budgets and emitted counts. Claim is released for orchestrator review; item remains in progress. Final exact-head npm/Bun release-gate results and run links are reported on the PR checks/description: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-brand/pull/27/checks . No merge or release is authorized."
